# What Prettier is not allowed to touch, on top of everything .gitignore
# already excludes (content-build passes both files to Prettier's own
# getFileInfo, so build output and node_modules need no entry here).

# The committed compendium source. This is not a style preference; the two
# checks would otherwise contradict each other permanently.
#
# `assets/packs/<name>/` is written by @foundryvtt/foundryvtt-cli's extractPack,
# via `npm run build:unpackdb`, and it emits 2-space JSON. The shared Prettier
# configuration is 4-space, so `content-build format` reports every one of the
# 1,597 documents, and `--write` reindents all of them — measured at 1,597 files
# changed, +70,110 / -70,589 lines, with no change of content anywhere.
#
# `lint:roundtrip` then fails, because it compares the committed bytes against
# what extracting the built packs produces — measured, on the reformatted tree,
# as 1,597 "committed bytes differ" problems. It runs inside `build:noci`, which
# is what release.yml builds a release from, so the reformat would not merely
# redden a check: it would stop every release until the packs were reverted.
#
# The round trip is the property CONTRIBUTING.md promises a contributor ("a git
# diff shows only your own edits") and the one the release depends on, so it is
# the one that owns these bytes. Anyone re-extracting the packs after editing a
# compendium in Foundry must be able to commit the result unmodified.
assets/packs/
